# Terraform state holds a DERIVED copy of the Talos PKI — derived, because the
# authoritative copy is the SOPS-encrypted machine-secrets.sops.json committed
# next to each cluster. That is the property that keeps state from being a
# second root secret (D12), and it is why local state is acceptable here at all.
#
# Derived is not harmless, though: an unencrypted state file on disk still
# contains key material. Never commit it.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Provider binaries; re-fetched by `terraform init`.
.terraform/

# The lock file is deliberately NOT ignored — it pins provider checksums, which
# is the same discipline as the version pins in versions.tf.

# Anything decrypted out of SOPS for a local run.
*.decrypted.json
*.auto.tfvars
